WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.820
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.120
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.400
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:08.660
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.480
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:19.460
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.620
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.060
Hello.

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.180
Hi, everybody.

10
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.840
It is AARM Part 2.

11
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.740
You know what that means.

12
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.540
Next week is the finale.

13
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:36.820
Finale.

14
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:38.860
Yeah.

15
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:39.660
Wow.

16
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:46.420
This is Season 9, Episode 25, written by Brent Forrester and directed by Dave Rogers.

17
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.060
And here's your summary.

18
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:55.280
Newly convinced that Philip is his son, Dwight unromantically proposes marriage to Angela.

19
00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.660
She says no.

20
00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:02.440
With the help of the documentary crew, Jim reassures Pam that she is more than enough for him.

21
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.040
Daryl's co-workers make one last request before he leaves.

22
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.020
Andy's singing dreams are shattered by Clay Aiken.

23
00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:17.560
And Dwight proposes again romantically to Angela.

24
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.520
And she says, yes.

25
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.880
Nothing says romance like a bullhorn.

26
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.040
That's one of my favorite parts of that scene.

27
00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:35.860
Well, everyone, I am holding my pockets mug again, but it's not because I have a soapbox today.

28
00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:39.940
It is because we have found Katie.

29
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.900
Katie, the maker of the pockets mug and the hummingbird mug.

30
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.220
Which I am holding right now as well.

31
00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:54.260
Kaya Goodwin from South Carolina went full mom detective, although she actually solved this case.

32
00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.160
So, slightly mom detective.

33
00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:56.860
Yes.

34
00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.900
She found Katie and Cassie was able to get in touch with her.

35
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.040
And everybody, Katie has an Etsy store for her pottery.

36
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.820
It's so beautiful.

37
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.480
Katie, you are so talented.

38
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.680
Jenna and I have already picked a few things we want to buy.

39
00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:11.640
It's true.

40
00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.340
We told Katie we would share about her Etsy shop.

41
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:23.400
Now, I believe she's willing to make more pocket mugs, but please be kind to her because she is just one gal making amazing pottery.

42
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.840
So, we don't want to overwhelm her.

43
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.100
With pocket mugs and hummingbird mugs.

44
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.520
You have to be patient.

45
00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.420
She makes everything herself.

46
00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:32.160
Yes.

47
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.100
Her Etsy shop is called Ravens and Widow, and we will link to it in our stories.

48
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.120
We sure will.

49
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.620
Cheers, lady.

50
00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:40.180
Cheers.

51
00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:53.220
Let's talk about the next acapella sensation celebrity judges, Aaron Rodgers, Clay Aiken, and Santi Gold.

52
00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.080
Can you believe it?

53
00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:56.040
We got these three?

54
00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.140
Amazing.

55
00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:03.240
So, when we got the script for this, when we did the table read, there were just like placeholders.

56
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.500
It was like pop star, country star, and athlete.

57
00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.780
And we found Santi Gold and Clay Aiken through Allison Jones.

58
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.480
But our own Brian Baumgartner is how we got Aaron Rodgers.

59
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.680
That's true.

60
00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:21.320
Because he had met Aaron at like a celebrity golf tournament or something.

61
00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.860
And Aaron Rodgers was a huge fan of The Office.

62
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.200
Like super fan.

63
00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.040
Super fan.

64
00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.300
He even came to set one time.

65
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.260
Remember when we were filming and he wanted to take pictures with all of us?

66
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:33.640
Yes.

67
00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:42.820
So, after the table read, Brian went to Greg and the producers and was like, hey, how about athlete is Aaron Rodgers?

68
00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.620
I mean, he would flip out to do this.

69
00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.360
And that is how we got Aaron Rodgers.

70
00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:57.700
Who, by the way, had just recently led the Green Bay Packers to victory in the Super Bowl and was the Super Bowl and NFL season MVP for that season.

71
00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:04.360
Yeah, you know, I have a little bit of an embarrassing story of when I first met Aaron.

72
00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.060
Okay.

73
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.460
So, Brian had done the golf tournament with him.

74
00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:08.740
Yeah.

75
00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.500
And they became friends.

76
00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:15.360
And I don't know if it was like a few weeks later or what, but Brian texted me and was like, hey, my friend's in town.

77
00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.580
We're going to go have dinner.

78
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:17.920
Do you want to join us?

79
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.920
I'm going to get a group of people together for dinner.

80
00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.040
I was like, sure.

81
00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.000
Sounds great.

82
00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.300
All I knew was his friend played sports.

83
00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:25.200
Right?

84
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:25.720
That's it.

85
00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.040
Brian didn't say anything else in the text.

86
00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.220
So I go to this dinner.

87
00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:39.240
And man, oh, man, am I noticing people like from every walk of life tripping over themselves to say hi to Brian's friend.

88
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:39.820
Uh-huh.

89
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.560
And I'm sitting next to him at dinner.

90
00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.060
And we're talking about work and stuff.

91
00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.540
And I go, so you play football?

92
00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.980
And he said, I do.

93
00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.520
And I said, that's so fun.

94
00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.280
That's really cool.

95
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.360
And I was like, what position do you play?

96
00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.100
He said, I'm a quarterback.

97
00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.020
And I go, wow.

98
00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.760
That's like big time.

99
00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.760
And then we don't really talk any more about it.

100
00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.020
Uh-huh.

101
00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:01.400
You know?

102
00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.740
We just talk about all kinds of other stuff.

103
00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.160
And this is when I had just started dating Josh.

104
00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.700
And the next day, he and I are on the phone.

105
00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.700
And he was like, how was your dinner with Brian and his friends?

106
00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:12.700
I said, so fun.

107
00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.180
I met such a nice guy.

108
00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:20.720
He's, I think he's a, oh, he's a quarterback for, I think, Seattle.

109
00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.320
Something with a bird.

110
00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:23.960
Maybe a hawk.

111
00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:24.720
Uh-huh.

112
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.200
And he goes, what's his name?

113
00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:27.620
And I said, Aaron.

114
00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.220
And he goes, no, no, no.

115
00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.160
There's no quarterback named Aaron for Seattle.

116
00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.380
He goes, I go, well, I think he's a pretty big deal.

117
00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.480
Because people were really excited to meet him.

118
00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.880
And then he goes, is it Aaron Rodgers, Aaron?

119
00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.260
And I said, yes, that's it.

120
00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:46.330
And he goes, oh, my God, no idea.

121
00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.690
He was just so nice and just unassuming.

122
00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:54.390
And anyway, I didn't know he was the quarterback for Green Bay.

123
00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:59.770
Well, I have a really fun audio clip for later in the episode.

124
00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:06.610
Because there was somebody else who also did not know who he was when they met him on our set that day.

125
00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:07.190
Oh, yeah.

126
00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.070
I'll save it.

127
00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.810
But it made me chuckle.

128
00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:14.370
Well, I'm a huge football fan, a football person.

129
00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.370
And I remember when he came to set.

130
00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:20.870
And I was just so tickled that he was so excited to take a picture with me.

131
00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:21.350
Yeah.

132
00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:24.010
You know, because I was like, you're Aaron Rodgers.

133
00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:28.010
Oh, there were so many fantasy football teams on our show.

134
00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.270
The whole set was so excited to have him visit.

135
00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.750
It's very true.

136
00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:37.010
Well, I'm excited to talk about another big guest star from this episode.

137
00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:41.610
It's our Fast Fact number two, and it is Santi Gold.

138
00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.710
Angela, we have a story about her.

139
00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:49.530
We were at a benefit fundraiser where she was performing.

140
00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.610
Yes, we got pretty excited.

141
00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:52.890
This is recently.

142
00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.330
This is, you know, a long time since she's been on the show.

143
00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:55.830
Yeah.

144
00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.710
This was just a few years ago, you guys.

145
00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.370
It was.

146
00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:01.090
First of all, I'll say we were right at the front.

147
00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.810
Like, we were right at the lip of the stage.

148
00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.110
We were dancing hardcore.

149
00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:05.030
Yeah, we were.

150
00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.730
She was playing Creator, my favorite song.

151
00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:10.130
And can we have it, by the way?

152
00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:11.310
Could we listen to some of that?

153
00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:11.690
Oh, my gosh.

154
00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:11.990
Yes.

155
00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:12.470
Can we?

156
00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:13.550
Can we play a little bit of it?

157
00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:14.310
I'd like to.

158
00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:18.590
Because I want you to understand, this is what Angela and I are rocking out to at, like,

159
00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.290
the front of this performance.

160
00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:21.810
The very front of the stage.

161
00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:22.110
Yes.

162
00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:54.480
Okay, so that is one of my songs I listen to when I want to feel like a badass boss lady.

163
00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.020
That's right.

164
00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.240
So we are two badass boss ladies.

165
00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.100
We are rocking out at the foot of the stage.

166
00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.260
And she says, everybody, come up.

167
00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:01.720
Come up.

168
00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.960
Come on stage and dance with me.

169
00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.480
We're like, we will.

170
00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:06.480
We're like, heck yeah.

171
00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.940
We start to mount the stage.

172
00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.060
And a big, beefy guy.

173
00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.260
He was a bouncer.

174
00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.280
Like a bouncer person.

175
00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:13.700
Yeah.

176
00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.940
Who worked at the venue was like, you will not be going on stage.

177
00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.740
And she was like, you are.

178
00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:19.680
Come on up on stage.

179
00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.700
We're like, she's saying we can go.

180
00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.800
And he's like, I'm saying you cannot.

181
00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.380
We almost got thrown out.

182
00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:29.400
I mean, one or two gals made it up on stage.

183
00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:30.180
We didn't.

184
00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.020
I was jealous.

185
00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:35.200
He pretty much, like, just gently picked me up and set me on the ground.

186
00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:37.120
He shut it down pretty quickly.

187
00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:41.920
But he was like, I will ask you ladies to leave if you do not stop trying to climb on

188
00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:42.520
the stage.

189
00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.000
I was like, oh no, we don't want to get thrown out.

190
00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.540
We don't want to get thrown out.

191
00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.180
Also, you guys, we were totally sober.

192
00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.220
We were.

193
00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.720
We were just really excited.

194
00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:52.940
She said, come up on stage.

195
00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:53.660
She did.

196
00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.580
But I know Santi.

197
00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.680
And she's an amazing person.

198
00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.220
And I traded text messages with her.

199
00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:04.680
And she said that she would send in audio clips for this episode.

200
00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:06.240
Here's the first one.

201
00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.020
She's going to tell us how she got her job on The Office.

202
00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.440
Oh my God.

203
00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.320
I just watched the link that you sent me.

204
00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.560
It's so funny.

205
00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:15.640
He's so great.

206
00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:23.220
And so, yeah, I was a huge fan of The Office.

207
00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:27.580
From the beginning of The Office, I was a fan of The Office when it was just the UK version

208
00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.260
of The Office.

209
00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.960
And then when it turned to the US version, I remember it was so different.

210
00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:38.200
But yet, I don't want to say funnier, but it kind of was.

211
00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.660
It was just so good.

212
00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:42.020
And so from the very beginning, I was watching it.

213
00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.240
And I had seen pretty much every episode.

214
00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:49.960
So what happened was, it was like I had been touring for quite a while.

215
00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:54.600
And I wanted to do something just that seemed fresh and new, something that I didn't know

216
00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.020
how to do.

217
00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:55.860
And that seemed fun.

218
00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.920
So I started taking some acting classes.

219
00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:08.940
And I went on, I think it was my very first audition was for Anchorman 2.

220
00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:16.420
And I went, and the casting agent, she said that I did really, really well.

221
00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.360
And she really liked me.

222
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:23.080
And then she was like, but because I had never acted before, the director wanted to go with

223
00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.780
someone who had more experience.

224
00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:27.780
So, you know, so I didn't get that.

225
00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:29.500
But she was like, really nice.

226
00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:32.040
So she called me very shortly after.

227
00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.280
And she's like, but would you want to come on The Office?

228
00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:35.780
And I couldn't believe it.

229
00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:38.300
I was like, that was like my dream.

230
00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:42.220
Like, because I just really wanted to be on something funny.

231
00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:45.300
Like, I don't think I even really wanted to ever be an actor.

232
00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.140
I just wanted to be on something funny.

233
00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.520
And The Office was like my number one wish liSt.

234
00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:54.320
So yeah, so, and I get to come on and just play myself.

235
00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.720
And so that's how that happened.

236
00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.220
And I was so excited about it.

237
00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.240
It was like a dream come true.

238
00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.240
Aw, so fun.

239
00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:06.540
Well, Dave said that she was super sweet and very talented.

240
00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.800
Dave also said she was so friendly and really warm.

241
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:14.780
But then when the camera started rolling, she had to just switch into just like pissed off.

242
00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:18.160
And he said it was a really funny thing to watch her have to do that.

243
00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.160
I can relate.

244
00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:24.820
Well, I have more audio clips from Santi that I'll play later in the episode.

245
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.520
But now, Angela, it's over to you for Fast Fact 3.

246
00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:28.640
Yes.

247
00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:32.380
Okay, so you guys know that I have been watching The Office A Look Back.

248
00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:35.360
It's the bonus feature on Disc 4, Season 9.

249
00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.740
I have some more to share from it.

250
00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:41.760
I am titling this first part, Feeling All the Feels.

251
00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.160
Okay.

252
00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.400
Here's the cast talking about the show.

253
00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.120
Very cheesy music.

254
00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.040
Like, just, wow.

255
00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:49.470
Mm-hmm.

256
00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:58.600
